00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:36.500
Well, somebody did.

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:55.059
Clark.

00:22:55.059 --> 00:22:59.059
Chloe told me about the girl in a group.

00:22:59.059 --> 00:23:01.059
It's a missed-up world.

00:23:01.059 --> 00:23:04.059
You know, Davis, it took a lot to go into that room full of screaming people.

00:23:04.059 --> 00:23:07.059
Who knows what you could have been running into?

00:23:07.059 --> 00:23:10.059
Yeah, well, I suppose it should be somewhat comforting to know the good guys.

00:23:10.059 --> 00:23:13.059
I don't know that good gossip spreads just as fast as bad.

00:23:13.059 --> 00:23:14.559
So you didn't save those people.

00:23:14.559 --> 00:23:15.559
Haven't we been over this?

00:23:15.559 --> 00:23:17.559
I'm not some larger-than-life hero.

00:23:17.559 --> 00:23:19.559
The truth is, I don't know what happened.

00:23:19.559 --> 00:23:22.559
But you do know more than what you've told me, don't you?

00:23:22.559 --> 00:23:26.559
I don't fish much, Clark, so why don't you just tell me what the hell you're after?

00:23:26.559 --> 00:23:27.559
What are you doing with the file?

00:23:27.559 --> 00:23:30.559
Stuff full of morbid pictures of murder victims?

00:23:30.559 --> 00:23:31.559
You broke into my locker.

00:23:31.559 --> 00:23:33.559
Collecting pictures of all the murder victims?

00:23:33.559 --> 00:23:35.059
It's a pretty strange habit, isn't it?

00:23:35.059 --> 00:23:37.559
Do you know how many murders in this city go itself?

00:23:37.559 --> 00:23:38.559
Every year, I show up.

00:23:38.559 --> 00:23:39.559
I take away the body's case closed.

00:23:39.559 --> 00:23:43.559
close. Maybe I want to do more than just clean up the mess after it's too late.

00:23:43.559 --> 00:23:47.559
Now the whole city refers to you as a hero, huh?

00:23:47.559 --> 00:23:51.559
Maybe I'd have an easier time believing all this if there was proof that that's actually what happened.

00:23:51.559 --> 00:23:55.559
Okay, you know what? I understand if you don't want to join the need-your-ticket-taped prey,

00:23:55.559 --> 00:23:59.559
but let me ask you a question. Are you really up in my face because you're trying to catch a killer

00:23:59.559 --> 00:24:01.559
or just because you're trying to hide something yourself?

00:24:01.559 --> 00:24:03.559
You'll try to turn this around on me.

00:24:03.559 --> 00:24:06.559
Why don't you take a second look at those photos?

00:24:06.559 --> 00:24:08.559
I'm not the only one that's hanging out of these crime scenes.

00:24:08.559 --> 00:24:09.539
There's another.

00:24:09.559 --> 00:24:11.559
figure in the background.

00:24:11.559 --> 00:24:16.549
You seem to be the city's own peeping town.

00:24:16.549 --> 00:24:18.549
I'm a reporter.

00:24:18.549 --> 00:24:20.549
It's my job.

00:24:20.549 --> 00:24:25.549
These photos were taken before any press could have made it to the scene.

00:24:25.549 --> 00:24:30.549
So, uh, next time you feel anxious to shine a line on things that don't make sense.

00:24:30.549 --> 00:25:01.640
I want to stay close for all.

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:03.640
Sharpening your pitchfork?

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:06.640
You're gonna lead a marauding posse. You better come prepared.

00:25:06.640 --> 00:25:09.640
Clark, you gave the police the names of my ISIS group?

00:25:09.640 --> 00:25:11.640
This group?

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:13.640
How could you use your powers to betray me like that?

00:25:13.640 --> 00:25:16.640
I didn't mean to go around you, Chloe, but you were so defensive.

00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:18.640
Like I've been defensive of you?

00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:22.640
Clerk, you don't get how much of my life I spend protecting your secret.

00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:25.640
And if you ever had enough courage to actually step forward,

00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:29.640
like the rest of these kids did, you would be the first one on that pyre.

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:33.640
How could you, of all people, be the ringleader for this witch hunt?

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:36.640
Chloe, you're taking the side of people that you hardly know.

00:25:36.640 --> 00:25:39.619
I would think after eight years of friendship you might be able to give me the benefit of the

00:25:39.640 --> 00:25:46.640
doubt. That works both ways. And your bonus features don't give you the right to trump

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:50.640
anyone else's judgment. Fine. We'll let the facts speak for themselves.

00:25:50.640 --> 00:25:56.329
These are the test results that Davis was trying to hide from me.

00:25:56.329 --> 00:25:57.329
Davis?

00:25:57.329 --> 00:26:03.000
Davis? I was thinking with your brainiac ability you might be able to make sense of the results.

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:11.480
Oh my God. The skin under the victim's nails is Davis's.

00:26:11.480 --> 00:26:36.319
Davis?

00:26:36.319 --> 00:27:00.079
You ready to catch killing?

00:27:00.079 --> 00:27:02.900
Yeah.

00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:16.900
So, how if you can get a dispatcher?

00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:18.900
It depends on the night.

00:27:18.900 --> 00:27:24.710
Some nights are busier than others.

00:27:24.710 --> 00:27:28.400
I bet you see a lot of horrible things, huh?

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:43.009
What's a 4-11?

00:27:43.009 --> 00:27:45.009
That's the reason you came along tonight.

00:27:45.009 --> 00:28:30.180
Stay here.

00:28:30.180 --> 00:29:21.329
His ambulance number is 17.

00:29:21.329 --> 00:29:26.329
I'm surprised you haven't enrolled the services of our friendly Martian on the force.

00:29:26.329 --> 00:29:28.329
Jones can't help us unless we have some hard proof.

00:29:28.329 --> 00:29:31.329
We need more than a few pieces of evidence that will rest in one.

00:29:31.329 --> 00:29:33.329
Yeah, and the evidence you have is an exactly conclusive.

00:29:33.329 --> 00:29:36.329
I mean, the victim could have easily just reached up and grabbed Davis when he was trying to help them.

00:29:36.329 --> 00:29:39.740
he was trying to help them.

00:29:39.740 --> 00:29:43.740
But I have to admit Davis would have the perfect setup.

00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:47.740
I mean, he attacks the people and then pretends to arrive at the scene to save them.

00:29:47.740 --> 00:29:53.799
I know it isn't easy.

00:29:53.799 --> 00:30:00.519
What, my perpetual knack for getting into lose-lose situations?

00:30:00.519 --> 00:30:01.519
Got it.

00:30:01.519 --> 00:30:03.519
Davis's ambulance just stopped.

00:30:03.519 --> 00:30:05.519
He answered a call a few minutes ago.

00:30:05.519 --> 00:30:10.930
Clark, that's Jimmy.

00:30:10.930 --> 00:30:47.430
What you do with Jimmy?

00:30:47.430 --> 00:30:50.990
Davis!

00:30:50.990 --> 00:30:53.970
Jimmy?

00:30:53.970 --> 00:31:09.980
Davis!

00:31:09.980 --> 00:31:10.980
You all right?

00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:18.069
Okay.

00:31:18.069 --> 00:31:19.069
See K.

00:31:19.069 --> 00:31:21.069
Jimmy, what's going on?

00:31:21.069 --> 00:31:22.069
It could be anywhere.

00:31:22.069 --> 00:31:24.069
Some sort of shadow creature.

00:31:24.069 --> 00:32:25.869
What?

00:32:25.869 --> 00:32:26.869
You okay?

00:32:26.869 --> 00:32:27.869
Yeah.

00:32:27.869 --> 00:32:28.869
Oh, good.

00:32:28.869 --> 00:33:32.759
I lost perspective.

00:33:32.759 --> 00:33:34.759
I can be a little stubborn.

00:33:34.759 --> 00:33:38.759
And I hate to admit it.

00:33:38.759 --> 00:33:41.759
There was a part of me that was really frustrated.

00:33:41.759 --> 00:33:44.759
You trusted someone else instead of me.

00:33:44.759 --> 00:33:51.539
It's funny how that happens when you go behind someone's back.

00:33:51.539 --> 00:33:55.009
My obsession had pushed me

00:33:55.009 --> 00:33:59.829
It's the line with you, Chloe.

00:33:59.829 --> 00:34:04.799
I'm really sorry.

00:34:04.799 --> 00:34:06.799
But you were protecting a killer.

00:34:06.799 --> 00:34:13.219
Yeah, well, and there's that.

00:34:13.219 --> 00:34:17.219
I guess I just didn't understand how you could hand over your trust so easily to people you didn't know.

00:34:17.219 --> 00:34:29.809
327.

00:34:29.809 --> 00:34:33.809
That's how many of the meteor infected I've profiled since ninth grade.

00:34:33.809 --> 00:34:36.809
And you know how many have actually saved?

00:34:36.809 --> 00:34:44.340
None.

00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:46.340
I guess I've been so busy rescuing people from them.

00:34:46.340 --> 00:34:48.340
I never looked at it from that angle.

00:34:48.340 --> 00:34:51.340
It's not just the damsels in distress that need saving, Clark.

00:34:51.340 --> 00:34:56.900
And you know, when I first thought that you were one of the meteor infected,

00:34:56.900 --> 00:34:58.900
I would have done anything to protect you.

00:34:58.900 --> 00:35:02.239
But I guess that's what scares me.

00:35:02.239 --> 00:35:07.389
I'm afraid that someday you're going to put your trust in the wrong person.

00:35:07.389 --> 00:35:31.690
Been waiting long?

00:35:31.690 --> 00:35:35.690
I don't know how to thank you for believing in me when I was up against the ropes.

00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:38.690
We all need someone to pitch a seat in her corner.

00:35:38.690 --> 00:35:43.690
Yeah, I guess, but most of the time it's not a possible murder suspect standing there.

00:35:43.690 --> 00:35:47.690
Davis, you were scared and paranoid. That's all.

00:35:47.690 --> 00:35:48.690
Seriously?

00:35:48.690 --> 00:35:52.690
Seriously? Backing someone who's actually innocent isn't much of a sacrifice.

00:35:52.690 --> 00:35:56.690
Besides, everything with you is so...

00:35:56.690 --> 00:35:58.690
So easy.

00:35:58.690 --> 00:36:01.690
Yeah. Easy.

00:36:01.690 --> 00:36:07.820
Have you ever felt that way with anyone before?

00:36:07.820 --> 00:36:12.849
What?

00:36:12.849 --> 00:36:15.869
With Jimmy.

00:36:15.869 --> 00:36:30.860
Chloe, I'm not trying to get between you and the rest of your life, but, uh...

00:36:30.860 --> 00:36:32.860
Davis, I help people.

00:36:32.860 --> 00:36:36.860
That's what I do. You know, this doesn't have to mean any more than that.

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:37.860
Yeah, but it does.

00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:47.829
Do you help me because of some personal code of ethics, or was there more to it than that?

00:36:47.829 --> 00:36:52.610
I shouldn't be here right now.

00:36:52.610 --> 00:36:54.610
Why? Because you feel guilty on something?

00:36:54.610 --> 00:36:59.610
No. And I'd like it to stay that way.

00:36:59.610 --> 00:37:05.360
I think it's best if I don't see you for a while.

00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:19.880
How could I've been so wrong about Davis?

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:22.880
This shadow guy confess to every killing in the last few weeks.

00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:26.880
Sometimes what we think is a good instinct is just our mind.

00:37:26.880 --> 00:37:28.880
Trying to convince ourselves of what we want to believe.

00:37:28.880 --> 00:37:29.880
Well, he may be able to believe.

00:37:29.880 --> 00:37:32.880
but that just means there's another psycho out there right around the corner.

00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:35.880
I've been here working every night and I still have to do more.

00:37:35.880 --> 00:37:40.349
You can't allow yourself to get caught.

00:37:40.349 --> 00:37:43.349
Combing through police blotters at your desk every night?

00:37:43.349 --> 00:37:46.349
Peeling back the sides of a bus in broad daylight.

00:37:46.349 --> 00:37:47.349
Speeding into a crowded bar.

00:37:47.349 --> 00:37:49.349
You're so fixated on being a hero.

00:37:49.349 --> 00:37:51.349
You're not paying attention to who might be watching.

00:37:51.349 --> 00:37:53.349
Is this your idea of a pep talk?

00:37:53.349 --> 00:37:55.349
It's not my identity that's at risk.

00:37:55.349 --> 00:37:58.349
Now, every day I have to run faster and faster interference

00:37:58.349 --> 00:38:00.349
on these mysterious Good Samaritan reports.

00:38:00.349 --> 00:38:01.349
Well, that just means I'm doing a pep talk.

00:38:01.349 --> 00:38:02.349
my job.

00:38:02.349 --> 00:38:06.329
You have to make sure no one sees my face.

00:38:06.329 --> 00:38:08.329
Well, you can't be sure of that.

00:38:08.329 --> 00:38:10.329
Unless you plan to put on a mask.

00:38:10.329 --> 00:38:12.329
You're joking, right?

00:38:12.329 --> 00:38:15.329
You are not in Smallville anymore, Clark.

00:38:15.329 --> 00:38:18.329
Metropolis has millions of people walking the streets,

00:38:18.329 --> 00:38:21.329
every one of them watching for a miracle.

00:38:21.329 --> 00:38:24.329
To change their lives, to give them hope.

00:38:24.329 --> 00:38:26.329
You are that miracle.

00:38:26.329 --> 00:38:29.329
And it's just a matter of time before someone discovers that.

00:38:29.329 --> 00:38:34.019
I'll be more careful.

00:38:34.019 --> 00:38:38.760
Hey, Clark.

00:38:38.760 --> 00:38:41.269
Clark.

00:38:41.269 --> 00:38:43.269
Perfect. Officer, listen.

00:38:43.269 --> 00:38:45.269
None of your fellow comrades, they don't want to give me the time of day,

00:38:45.269 --> 00:38:52.079
but you look like you're, uh, thinking outside of the box kind of guy.

00:38:52.079 --> 00:38:56.079
There's a, there's a mystery hero roaming the streets metropolis.

00:38:56.079 --> 00:39:00.079
Look, Scouts, honor. Out of nowhere, these tigers, they come floating through the air.

00:39:00.079 --> 00:39:02.079
And this Mr. Shadow guy, he gets knocked around like a ping pong ball.

00:39:02.079 --> 00:39:03.079
Slow down.

00:39:03.079 --> 00:39:06.079
Oh, Olsen, James Olson, photographer daily planet.

00:39:06.079 --> 00:39:11.079
Well, James, uh, adrenaline can play strange games with a person.

00:39:11.079 --> 00:39:12.079
No, no. He's...

00:39:12.079 --> 00:39:14.079
No, no, he's... he's real.

00:39:14.079 --> 00:39:16.079
I know it.

00:39:16.079 --> 00:39:17.079
I hope you're right.

00:39:17.079 --> 00:39:18.079
We could use the help.

00:39:18.079 --> 00:39:22.420
And when you get some hard evidence,

00:39:22.420 --> 00:39:24.420
I'll be more than glad to continue this conversation.

00:39:24.420 --> 00:39:28.920
Even in Mr. Olson.

00:39:28.920 --> 00:39:29.920
Mr. Kent.

00:39:29.920 --> 00:39:44.599
I'm gonna prove that this guy exists, C.K.

00:39:44.599 --> 00:40:15.869
He's out there.

00:40:15.869 --> 00:40:17.869
You look a little uncomfortable.

00:40:17.869 --> 00:40:19.869
You're not a lawyer.

00:40:19.869 --> 00:40:21.869
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:40:21.869 --> 00:40:26.150
Congratulations on your page one.

00:40:26.150 --> 00:40:33.050
It's nice to have your work recognized.

00:40:33.050 --> 00:40:34.050
After so many people.

00:40:34.050 --> 00:40:38.360
years being the good little boy in the shadows.

00:40:38.360 --> 00:40:41.360
You have more admirers than you think.

00:40:41.360 --> 00:40:46.360
My boss, Ms. Mercer, has been gathering a small group of talent if you're game.

00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:49.360
You've read my list of accomplishments.

00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:52.360
I'm not really interested in sharing top billing.

00:40:52.360 --> 00:40:55.360
Cut the bravado. You didn't commit all those murders.

00:40:55.360 --> 00:41:00.710
You're just a copycat looking for attention.

00:41:00.710 --> 00:41:05.710
Cops haven't found this yet, but we have security footage of you at an arcade during one of the crimes.

00:41:05.710 --> 00:41:10.710
It's a crime I'm sure you've studied if you were looking to mimic the real killer.

00:41:10.710 --> 00:41:16.239
You remember the nun at St. Vincent's crushed to death?

00:41:16.239 --> 00:41:20.239
That surveillance time code must have been wrong because that was me.

00:41:20.239 --> 00:41:22.239
Really?

00:41:22.239 --> 00:41:26.239
Then I suppose you can tell me where her missing onyx crucifix is.

00:41:26.239 --> 00:41:29.650
The one on the Rosary.

00:41:29.650 --> 00:41:31.650
You didn't kill her.

